# SerikaCord

Read `CLAUDE.md` (full guide) and `AGENTS.md` before making changes;
`docs/architecture/` has the realtime, data model, API, frontend and security
deep dives.

Safety:
- Canary's Postgres and Redis are PRODUCTION data shared with prod. No
  destructive SQL, no `drizzle-kit push`/`migrate`, no ad-hoc writes.
- Schema changes: additive + idempotent SQL in `drizzle/manual_*.sql` and
  `src/lib/db/schema.ts`; the owner applies them.
- Never test in public servers or with real users.
- Never push/tag/force-push. Never stash, reset, restore or commit the owner's
  uncommitted work; stage only your own paths.

Conventions:
- `gt("literal")` / `<T>` for every user-facing string.
- Theme colors via CSS variables (`var(--app-*)`), never hard-coded hex.
- One chat engine for channels and DMs (`useChatSession`, `MessageList`).
- Live events via `publishToChannel` / `publishToDm` / `fanoutToUsers`;
  registries via `processShared()`; bot/webhook/system messages call
  `messageSignals`.
- Models silently ignore unknown `find`/`findOne` filter keys.
- Webpack only, never Turbopack.

Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json`, `npx eslint <files>`,
`bun run test`, `bun run check:theme`; add a `## Unreleased` changelog bullet
for user-visible changes.
